  "notes": "Lumio Vision 7, 55\" / 139 cm (KTC ODM, Realtek chipset, device khardi, product KTC_LUMIO_4K_EU_23GV1), India\nGoogle TV 14 (Android 14, SDK 34), build UKRA.251202.032\nFirst Lumio list. Contributed by Subramanya GB.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> FORCE_SETUPWRAITH=1 tools/disable.sh examples/lumio-vision-7/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/lumio-vision-7/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx (disabled by launcher/build-and-install.sh after the\nnew launcher is confirmed Home). On this build setupwraith re-claims Home (.RecoveryActivity/.MainActivity)\nthe moment launcherx is off, and the shell cannot disable that component alone (SecurityException), so\nsetupwraith has to be disabled too (listed below). The active Wi-Fi here was system-owned (OwnerUid 1000),\nso disabling setupwraith did NOT drop Wi-Fi - but disable.sh's guard is conservative, hence\nFORCE_SETUPWRAITH=1. Disabling setupwraith may break Chromecast (mediashell reads device info from it);\nre-enable setupwraith to get casting back.\nLive TV / tuner app: com.realtek.tv (set as live_tv_package in config.xml, and hidden from the grid).\nNetflix (com.netflix.ninja) shipped already disabled on this unit.\nRemote app buttons (for config.xml app_keys): YouTube 190, Netflix 191, Prime Video 195, TL;DR 200.\nTested same day over Wireless debugging (classic port 5555 was already open): every HDMI/tuner input and\ninstalled app verified by screenshot; rebooted and the fork launcher came back as Home.\nAd tracking / Privacy Sandbox",
